548: 
549: ## IF.9. Exact face kernels and the remaining real attachment
550: 
551: Put \(C=2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda_0\). On the A face the kernel period is
552: \(g\). Its transverse line coordinate is \(V\), and its multiplier is
553: \[
554:                   C\epsilon^N q_*q_B^{-2}u_X^{-2}.       \tag{IF.27}
555: \]
556: On the B face the kernel is \(k=g h^{-b}\). Its source multiplier
557: and its multiplier on the literal transverse coordinate \(Y=Z^aV\)
558: are
559: \[
560:  (q_Au_Qu_P)^{-b},\qquad
561:           C\epsilon^N q_*q_A^{-2}u_Q^{-2}u_P^{-4}u_X^{-2}.       \tag{IF.28}
562: \]
563: These equalities follow directly from (IF.15): the second line is
564: \(g_V/(QP^2)^2\). Since the two critical values differ by
565: \(\epsilon\) times a nonzero unit, both transverse kernel
566: contractions have order \(N-2>0\) at their corresponding strict face.
567: All constants and source multipliers remain in (IF.27)--(IF.28).
568: They are not replaced by a formal valuation.
569: 
570: At E the source period \(h\) retains the actual compact elliptic
571: source fibre and its line holonomy. The scalar period has order \(N\)
572: and acts on the primitive chain (IF.26). Near H, both previously
573: kernel directions have nonzero image under the full-rank matrix
574: \(H_\infty\). Thus the period separation in the full-rank cones
575: controls the closures of both face norm shells; no additional
576: kernel is lost at that overlap.
577: 
578: These data give the local normal analytic collision quotient by
579: the same explicit lattice-and-norm-shell argument: use a logarithmic
580: fundamental parallelogram for the full lattice (IF.24), use the
581: strip inverse above to keep it in finitely many adjacent cones,
582: and absorb the bounded logarithms of the retained units by an
583: enlarged finite union. On A and B use the contracting transverse
584: shells (IF.27)--(IF.28), and on E use the actual elliptic-period
585: fundamental region and primitive chain. Their overlaps are the
586: same period maps, and the preceding nonzero H images keep their
587: closures in that enlarged union. This establishes the local
588: quotient with the stated boundary charts.
589: 
590: The global E-chain monodromy still carries its actual source-base
591: data. A small loop around the unselected collision has zero winding
592: of \(q_*\), so it fixes all \(N\) chain labels. A loop around the
593: separate selected value shifts labels by \(-nk\), and the inverse
594: cap cut at infinity shifts them by \(+nk\), for \(N=km\).
595: The latter two have \(k\) cycles of length \(m\). This is a
596: compatible list of branch locations; it does not itself construct
597: the missing selected-cusp attachment.
598: 
599: To complete the source return one still needs a real bordism
600: joining this collision/cap partial filling to the actual selected
601: I1 scalar trace, with its physical Euler line and normal
602: orientation. No full holomorphic selected corner, compact global
603: fourfold, signature, or return value is asserted in this note.
604: 
605: ## IF.10. The changed-origin partial attachment away from the selected disc
606: 
607: Fix disjoint source-base discs around the unselected collision at \(t=0\),
608: the selected value \(t=t_*(\epsilon)\), and the cap at infinity. The first
609: and last closures are disjoint from the selected disc for all sufficiently
610: small \(\epsilon\). Put \(N=km\), retain the actual \(n=\pm1\), and use
611: \[
612:  \tau=\frac{\log\epsilon}{2\pi i},\quad
613:  s_*=\frac{\log q_*}{2\pi i},\quad
614:  s_\infty=\frac{\log q_\infty}{2\pi i},\quad
615:  h=1-t_*(\epsilon)q_\infty,\qquad
616:  s_*=-s_\infty+\frac{\log h}{2\pi i}.                   \tag{IF.29}
617: \]
618: On the unselected collision bidisc \(q_*\) is a nonzero unit, so \(s_*\)
619: has one holomorphic branch on that full bidisc. On the cap polydisc \(h\)
620: is likewise a nonzero unit, with its chosen reference logarithm.
621: 
622: On the universal parameter cover the actual ordinary-to-cap map and
623: the actual positive parameter-deck square are
624: \[
625:  F_\tau=F_0+nk\,\tau s_\infty\delta,\qquad
626:  R_{\rm ord}=q_*^{nk},\quad R_{\rm cap}=h^{nk},\qquad
627:  F_{\tau+1}R_{\rm ord}=R_{\rm cap}F_\tau.               \tag{IF.30}
628: \]
629: These are the admitted cap's norm and cochain formulas, with the current
630: source and the transported full \(F_0\) of IF.3. The source and line
631: characters are not changed. Define
632: \[
633:  o_{\rm ord}=nk\,\tau s_*\delta,\qquad
634:  o_{\rm cap}=nk\,\tau\frac{\log h}{2\pi i}\delta,\qquad
635:  \eta=\zeta-o_{\rm ord}.
636: \]
637: The exact overlap is
638: \[
639:                 F_\tau+o_{\rm ord}-o_{\rm cap}=F_0.    \tag{IF.31}
640: \]
641: After a positive parameter turn the old ordinary chart is identified
642: by \(R_{\rm ord}\). Its change is exactly the change of \(o_{\rm ord}\);
643: therefore \(\eta\) has identity parameter deck. The cap coordinates
644: have the same property. This retains the closing arrow: neither
645: \(R_{\rm ord}\) nor \(R_{\rm cap}\) is silently set equal to one in
646: the old chart.
647: 
648: Every source period and line lift commutes with these base-only scalar
649: translations. Hence in the new ordinary coordinate the full periods
650: are exactly (IF.15), including all their units. Moreover positive
651: \(q_A\) or \(q_B\) continuation in the collision bidisc leaves \(s_*\)
652: unchanged. Thus the new collision coordinate has no additional
653: source-base chain deck there. The fan of IF.8 may therefore be
654: constructed directly in \(\eta\), and its quotient of IF.9 has the
655: pure parameter deck just proved. On its punctured parameter part
656: this is an actual isomorphism to the prescribed family, using
657: (IF.30), not an assertion that a fractional scalar power extends in
658: the old \(V\) coordinate.
659: 
660: The cap chain is constructed in \(\zeta_{\rm cap}-o_{\rm cap}\).
661: The actual primitive generator is
662: \[
663:  H=A^uB^w=\epsilon^k r_0H_0,\qquad nu+mw=1,
664:  \qquad H^m=B,\quad H^n=A ,
665: \]
666: with the actual admitted source and line maps. The displayed Bezout
667: equation is the literal exponent identity for \(A=H^n,B=H^m\).
668: Thus its node chart shift is
669: \(k\), and \(A\) has signed shift \(nk\). The source and finite
670: root maps in \(H_0\) are retained. The chain equations and all line
671: frame transitions are (IF.26), with \(H\) acting by that shift and
672: by its actual source/line map. A nonzero iterate changes the index,
673: so the action is free and properly discontinuous also at
674: \(\epsilon=0\).
675: 
676: On the cap annulus positive \(q_\infty\) continuation changes
677: \(s_*\) by \(-1\); the new ordinary vertical coordinate consequently
678: has the factor \(\epsilon^{nk}\). This is exactly \(A\)'s chain
679: shift and its retained \(A_0\) arrow. The cap unit \(h^{nk}\) acts
680: on a node chart by
681: \((X_j,Y_j)\mapsto(h^{nk}X_j,h^{-nk}Y_j)\); it is an extending
682: unit even though its central value is now \(1-q_\infty\), rather
683: than the constant one of the source-zero calculation. Its origin
684: change has been retained in (IF.30)--(IF.31).
685: 
686: On each remaining ordinary source-base chart, away from the selected
687: disc and these two special pieces, the source and Cartier line are
688: smooth over the full parameter disc. Use their full chain with the
689: actual source/line period. On angular overlaps the affine cochains
690: are exactly those already prescribed by \(F_0\); the only nonzero
691: integral base continuation is the signed cap shift just displayed.
692: The collision overlap has zero such continuation. Consequently
693: the ordinary chains, the collision fan in \(\eta\), and the cap
694: chain glue by literal extending source/line maps. This constructs
695: the partial family over the complement of the selected source-base
696: disc.
697: 
698: The relative regularization is by primitive determinant-one cones,
699: and the protected face charts are the actual smooth source/chain
700: charts. The total complex fourfold is therefore smooth. The map
701: to the epsilon disc may have a singular central fibre; smoothness
702: here refers to the total space and does not replace that map by a
703: submersion.
704: 
705: Properness over a closed smaller parameter disc follows from the
706: finite compact fundamental covers already described: collision
707: cones and face shells in IF.9, finitely many node/middle chain
708: charts on every ordinary compact source patch, and one finite
709: fundamental chain segment for \(H\) on the cap. A finite source-base
710: cover suffices. Every overlap is the actual biholomorphic map
711: (IF.31), so these compact covers produce a compact inverse image.
712: The only retained real boundary is over the boundary circle of the
713: deleted selected disc.
714: 
715: This is the partial attachment used in the next step. It provides
716: no filling of that last boundary and no return invariant. The exact
717: remaining morphism is its gluing to the selected-cusp scalar trace
718: with the physical Euler line and its normal orientation.
719: 
